        # Para 13
        "Yet it is not merely the sadness of this spectacle for the onlooker; there is the dull, intolerable malaise felt by the person who sees himself reduced to living as if he were effectively indistinguishable from his functions; and this malaise is enough to show that there is here a frightful error or abuse of interpretation which an increasingly inhuman social order, together with a philosophy that is equally inhuman (and which, if it preformed that order, has subsequently modeled itself upon it), have combined to instill into defenseless minds.",
        
