        "I have had occasion to write that, provided it is taken in its metaphysical and not its physical sense, the distinction between the full and the empty seemed to me more fundamental than that between the one and the many. This remark assumes its full significance here. Life in a world centered upon the idea of function is exposed to despair; it leads straight to despair, because in reality this world is empty, because it rings hollow. If it resists despair, it is only to the extent that certain secret powers, which it is unable to conceptualize or acknowledge, are at work within this existence and on its behalf. Only, this basic blindness inevitably tends to restrict the possible operation of these powers and ultimately to deprive them of their ground of support.",
        
