        # Para 25
        "I hold, therefore, for my part, that the ontological exigence can be reduced to silence only by an arbitrary, dictatorial act that mutilates spiritual life at its very root. The fact remains that this act is possible—our conditions of existence are such that we can genuinely believe we are performing it; and this is what must not be forgotten."
